Time to combine everything — variables, flexbox, grid, positioning, and pseudo-elements — into a real **product landing page**. A landing page has one job: convince the visitor to click the button, so every visual decision serves clarity and trust.

### The hero section
A hero is the full-width first impression: a bold headline, a supporting line, and a call-to-action button. Build it as a centered flex column so it adapts to any screen height:

```css
.hero {
  min-height: 80vh;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  text-align: center;
}
```
Flexbox is the right tool here because the hero is a single stack centered in both axes — a one-directional component.

### Buttons that feel alive
```css
.btn {
  background: var(--accent);
  transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
}
.btn:hover {
  transform: translateY(-2px);
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
}
```
Transitions turn an instant state change into a smooth one. A `0.2s` ease feels snappy and responsive — long transitions feel sluggish.

### The features grid
```css
.features {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
  gap: 24px;
}
```
This one-liner is responsive without a single media query: columns shrink until they hit 240px, then wrap onto a new row. Grid handles the two-dimensional layout; flexbox and variables handle the details inside each card.

### Decorative pseudo-elements
```css
.feature-card {
  position: relative;
}
.feature-card::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 4px;
  background: var(--accent);
}
```
An absolutely positioned `::before` (anchored by the `relative` card) draws a colored accent bar across each card's top edge — visual polish with zero extra HTML.

### Media queries for fine-tuning
Grid absorbs most of the responsiveness, but a media query lets you tune typography and padding at small widths:

```css
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .hero h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; }
  .hero { padding: 32px 16px; }
}
```

### Checklist before you submit
- CSS variables for colors and spacing (theming)
- Flexbox for hero centering
- Grid + `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(...))` for the features row
- `:hover` + `transition` on the button
- Responsive columns that wrap automatically

Build the hero first, then the features grid, then polish the interactions — the same order you'd build a real product page.

